## CI/CD

- Pin CI action/plugin versions to immutable references (commit SHA, digest), not mutable tags.
- Never hardcode secrets in CI configs. Use platform secret management.
- Minimize default CI token permissions. Use read-only where possible.
- Run security scanning in CI. Fail on HIGH/CRITICAL.
- Run dependency audit in CI. Fail on HIGH/CRITICAL.
- Use frozen lockfile mode in CI — never install without it.
- Use peer review + automated quality gates (tests, scans) as deployment control.
- Run typecheck + lint + test in CI — all must pass before merge.
- Pin runtime to current LTS version.
- Use preview/staging environments to test before production.
- Separate environment configs: development, staging, production. Never share databases across environments.
- Never run AI agents against production databases.

## Dependency Upgrades

- Before major upgrade: read the migration guide/changelog.
- Identify breaking changes and search for affected APIs in codebase.
- Upgrade one dependency at a time. Run full test suite after each.
- Use official codemods when available.
- Update lockfile. Verify build succeeds.